        <article><![CDATA[<p>Open the <strong>Doppel TI Configuration</strong> list. If it is empty, click <strong>New</strong>; otherwise open the existing record (only one is allowed).</p>
<ol><li><strong>Connection</strong>: choose the API version, enter the credentials and click <strong>Test Connectivity</strong>. Changed connection settings can only be saved after a successful test.</li><li><strong>Import</strong>: choose which Doppel products to import, how many days of past alerts the first import fetches, and how often the import runs. The scheduled import switches on automatically once the configuration is saved with a successful connection test.</li><li><strong>Indicator rules</strong>: choose which alerts also become Threat Intelligence indicators.</li><li><strong>Threat Lookup</strong>: choose which Doppel queue states make a lookup result Malicious.</li></ol>
<p><strong>Caution:</strong> the import runs as a scheduled job. Choose an interval that suits your data volume and instance load; every 60 minutes is a sensible start.</p>
<p>Click <strong>Submit</strong> or <strong>Update</strong>, then mark this task complete.</p>]]></article>
